<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Choose a principal, a rate and a time so that the simple interest is exactly Ksh <m>{6000}</m>. Your rate must be from <m>5\%</m> to <m>20\%</m> per annum and your time from <m>1</m> to <m>6</m> years. Many answers are correct.</p><p><m>P =</m> Ksh <fillin characters="10" name="ansP"/> </p><p><m>R =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ansR"/> % per annum </p><p><m>T =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="ansT"/> years </p><p/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Any <m>P</m>, <m>R</m> and <m>T</m> inside the rules with <m>PRT = 100 \times {6000}</m> is correct. Choose <m>R</m> and <m>T</m> first, then <m>P = \dfrac{100 \times {6000}}{RT}</m>.</p><p>For example, <m>R = 10</m> and <m>T = 3</m> give <m>P = \dfrac{100 \times {6000}}{30} = {20\,000}</m>. Check: <m>\dfrac{{20\,000} \times 10 \times 3}{100} = {6000}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>20000</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>10</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>